  summary  = {WHO monograph on the fresh or dried leaves of Ocimum sanctum L. (Lamiaceae), i.e. Ocimum tenuiflorum (tulsi/holy basil). Posology: daily dosage 6-12 g of crude drug as a decoction. This is the only regulatory-tier posology found for tulsi leaf as a water preparation - the EMA has no monograph, and the clinical literature uses standardised extracts or swallowed leaf powder rather than a tea.}
}

