  note     = {REF-3201},
  study_type = {traditional},
  summary  = {University of Wisconsin Extension horticulture article on dill (Anethum graveolens). Gives the seed harvest stage: "The seed heads can be cut from the stalks when the seeds are fully developed but before they have turned brown." Cited for harvest-readiness timing of the seed (the seeds shatter once fully ripe).}
